$abs(vb(a) times vb(b))$ is the area of the parallelogram formed by $vb(a)$ and $vb(b)$, so the triangle $O A B$ with $vb(a) = arrow(O A)$, $vb(b) = arrow(O B)$ has area $(1)/(2) abs(vb(a) times vb(b))$. Fixing $vb(a)$ and restricting to $vb(x) perp vb(a)$, the map $vb(x) mapsto vb(a) times vb(x)$ scales $vb(x)$ by $abs(vb(a))$ and rotates it by $(pi)/(2)$ within the plane orthogonal to $vb(a)$.
